<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<Defs>
  <!--
    The Medic armor's active, granted by the armor's CompProperties_AbilitiesApparel and fed
    by the medicine suite beside it (ThingDefs_Misc/Warcasket_Medic.xml). The rules live in
    MedicWarcasket.Ability_MechaniteDressing; the walk, warmup, beam and warmdown job in
    MedicWarcasket.JobDriver_MechaniteDressing (JobDefs/MechaniteDressing.xml).

    range is unset and requireLineOfSight off on purpose: the click is not range-limited, the
    pilot walks to the patient and the job driver enforces distance and sight at
    distanceToTarget. 2.9 is how close the pilot gets before the dressing starts (RimWorld's
    x.9 radii put it on the settings grid); the range setting moves it.
    castTime 60 (1 s) is the warmup before the stream connects, and cooldownTime 0 lets
    dressings follow one another: the kits a dressing draws are the limit, not a timer. Both,
    distanceToTarget and the extension's ticksPerTend are mod settings defaulting to these
    values.

    DressingExtension: ticksPerTend is the time the beam spends on each wound at a
    MedicalTendSpeed of 1.0, divided by the pilot's stat floored at minTendSpeed, as vanilla
    divides its tend duration (the class header has the call path). Vanilla's curve is 0.4 plus
    0.06 per Medicine level: Medicine 10 is 1.0 (the setting), Medicine 20 with the shoulders'
    +0.25 is 1.85, and an unskilled pilot's 0.4 floors at 0.5, twice the setting, so a weak medic
    cannot hold a patient under fire for long. maxPotency clips the medicine's potency before
    vanilla's quality formula (the pilot's MedicalTendQuality times the potency, clamped to the
    medicine's quality cap): at glitterworld's 1.6 the 1.3 cap is reached at Medicine 6 (5 with
    the helmet's +0.10) and skill stops counting there; clipped to 1.3, the cap's own value,
    it is reached at Medicine 8 (7 with the helmet), so skill counts for longer without
    costing an unskilled pilot much: four fifths of a doctor's quality with the same kit below
    the cap. Industrial's 1.0 is under the ceiling and tended as vanilla would. warmdownTicks is
    the pilot's hold after the beam ends, over which the glow fades. VEF ignores the extension.
    minTendSpeed, maxPotency and warmdownTicks have no setting.

    Sounds: warmupStartSound plays once as the warmup begins and warmupSound loops through it,
    both VEF fields; both are placeholders for the sound pass.

    Targeting: an explicit targetingParametersList entry rather than targetMode's generated
    one, to keep mechanoids and the pilot out (canTargetSelf is honoured by the vanilla
    Targeter). Faction is not checked, so a downed raider can be dressed before capture.

    No iconPath: the mod settings write the configured medicine's uiIcon onto def.icon at
    startup, so the gizmo, the cursor and the settings header show that item's icon until
    custom ability art lands.
  -->
  <VEF.Abilities.AbilityDef>
    <defName>MDWC_MechaniteDressing</defName>
    <label>mechanite dressing</label>
    <description>Stream medicine-laden mechanites onto a nearby person or animal to tend their wounds where they stand, most urgent first. Tend quality depends on the pilot's medical skill and the medicine used, and the skill sets the pace.

Reloads with medicine.</description>
    <abilityClass>MedicWarcasket.Ability_MechaniteDressing</abilityClass>
    <jobDef>MDWC_MechaniteDressing</jobDef>
    <jobReportString>Applying a mechanite dressing.</jobReportString>
    <targetMode>Pawn</targetMode>
    <targetingParametersList>
      <li>
        <canTargetPawns>true</canTargetPawns>
        <canTargetHumans>true</canTargetHumans>
        <canTargetAnimals>true</canTargetAnimals>
        <canTargetMechs>false</canTargetMechs>
        <canTargetSelf>false</canTargetSelf>
        <canTargetBuildings>false</canTargetBuildings>
        <canTargetLocations>false</canTargetLocations>
      </li>
    </targetingParametersList>
    <distanceToTarget>2.9</distanceToTarget>
    <requireLineOfSight>false</requireLineOfSight>
    <castTime>60</castTime>
    <cooldownTime>0</cooldownTime>
    <warmupStartSound>MechSerumUsed</warmupStartSound>
    <warmupSound>Interact_Tend</warmupSound>
    <showUndrafted>true</showUndrafted>
    <modExtensions>
      <li Class="MedicWarcasket.DressingExtension">
        <ticksPerTend>60</ticksPerTend>
        <minTendSpeed>0.5</minTendSpeed>
        <maxPotency>1.3</maxPotency>
        <warmdownTicks>60</warmdownTicks>
      </li>
    </modExtensions>
  </VEF.Abilities.AbilityDef>
</Defs>
